# Which Devanagari character arrives as which byte of hien's alphabet.
#
# The machine reads one byte at a time. A caller writes code points --
# U+0928 for na -- and the engine turns each into a byte before any
# rule sees it, through one Windows Western list, keeping the low byte
# of anything else. Devanagari is nowhere in that list, so U+0928
# arrived as 0x28, an open bracket, and a Hindi word came out as a row
# of punctuation. That is the whole of why Hindi spoke gibberish.
#
# Written by tools/hien-devanagari.py, which also points the alphabet
# at these bytes: the two have to agree exactly, so one file holds the
# facts and writes both.

0905 80  # da_ says a
0906 81  # daa says Aa
0907 8a  # di says i
0908 8c  # dii says I
0909 93  # du says u
090a 94  # duu says U
090b 95  # dri says r, wants a vocalic r
090f 96  # de says e
0910 97  # dai says E
0913 98  # do says o
0914 99  # dau says O
0915 9a  # dka says k
0916 9c  # dkha says k, wants an aspirated k
0917 9d  # dga says g
0918 a1  # dgha says g, wants a breathy g
0919 a2  # dnga says G
091a a3  # dca says C
091b a4  # dcha says C, wants an aspirated ch
091c a5  # dja says J
091d a6  # djha says J, wants a breathy j
091e a7  # dnya says n, wants a palatal n
091f a8  # dTa says t, wants a retroflex t
0920 a9  # dTha says t, wants an aspirated retroflex t
0921 aa  # dDa says d, wants a retroflex d
0922 ab  # dDha says d, wants a breathy retroflex d
0923 ac  # dNa says n, wants a retroflex n
0924 ad  # dta says t
0925 ae  # dtha says t, wants an aspirated t
0926 af  # dda says d
0927 b0  # ddha says d, wants a breathy d
0928 b1  # dna says n
092a b2  # dpa says p
092b b3  # dpha says f
092c b4  # dba says b
092d b5  # dbha says b, wants a breathy b
092e b6  # dma says m
092f b7  # dya says y
0930 b8  # dra says r
0932 b9  # dla says l
0935 ba  # dva says v
0936 bb  # dsha says S
0937 bc  # dSha says S, wants a retroflex sh
0938 bd  # dsa says s
0939 be  # dha says h
093e bf  # dmaa says Aa
093f c0  # dmi says i
0940 c1  # dmii says I
0941 c2  # dmu says u
0942 c3  # dmuu says U
0943 c4  # dmri says r, wants a vocalic r
0947 c5  # dme says e
0948 c6  # dmai says E
094b c7  # dmo says o
094c c8  # dmau says O
0902 c9  # danu says n, wants a nasal on the vowel before
0901 ca  # dcandra says n, wants a nasal on the vowel before
0903 cb  # dvisarga says h
094d cc  # dvirama says GAP
0964 cd  # ddanda says GAP
